                  </td>
                  <td align="right" valign="bottom" width="74">365,750,000</td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr style="keep-together.within-page:always;">
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(3)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" style="keep-together.within-page:always;" valign="top" width="214">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">2390019-Research and Development<span class="DottedLeaders"/>
                  </s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td align="right" valign="bottom" width="74">54,000,000</td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr style="keep-with-next.within-page:always;">
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td colspan="6" valign="top" width="312">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">Provisions:</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">1.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The funds appropriated in Schedule (1) shall be used to provide incentives for the Distributed Electricity
                  Backup Assets Program.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">2.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The funds appropriated in Schedule (2) shall be used as follows:</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em
                  0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(a)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$133,000,000 shall be used for administrative costs to support the deployment of
                  			 charging infrastructure for light-duty electric vehicles.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(b)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$57,000,000 shall be used to support the deployment of equitable-at-home charging infrastructure.</s></p><div
                  style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(c)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$47,500,000 shall be used for administrative costs to support the deployment of charging and hydrogen
                  refueling infrastructure for zero-emission drayage trucks.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(d)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$84,550,000 shall be used to support the deployment of charging and hydrogen
                  			 refueling infrastructure for clean trucks, buses, and off-road equipment, including, but not limited to, construction
                  and agricultural vehicles and equipment.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(e)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$43,700,000 shall be used to support emerging opportunities that include support of zero-emission
                  aviation, locomotive, and marine vehicles and vehicle-grid integration efforts.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">3.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The funds in this item shall be available for encumbrance or expenditure by the State Energy Resources
                  Conservation and Development Commission until June 30, 2029, and shall be available for liquidation until June 30, 2033.</s></p><div
                  style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">4.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The Department of Finance may adjust the amounts in Provision 2 to provide up to $3,250,000 to the
                  State Energy Resources Conservation and Development Commission for administrative costs to fund zero-emission school bus charging
                  or refueling infrastructure and related activities.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">5.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">With the funds appropriated in Schedule (2), the State Energy Resources Conservation and Development
                  Commission shall administer a program to fund projects consistent with Section 44272 of the Health and Safety Code, and consistent
                  with the following requirements:</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(a)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The commission may add these funds to existing competitively awarded agreements if existing competitive
                  agreements are consistent with the use of funds described in Provision 1 of this item.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(b)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The commission may adopt guidelines or other standards for this program at a commission business
                  meeting following at least one public workshop. The Administrative Procedure Act (Chapter 3.5 (commencing with Section 11340)
                  of Part 1 of Division 3 of Title 2 of the Government Code) does not apply to guidelines or other standards for the program
                  adopted at a commission business meeting.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">6.</td>
                  <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">The funds
                  			 appropriated in Schedule (3) shall be used as follows:</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(a)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$23,400,000 shall be used for Local Assistance for the Long Duration Energy Storage Program.</s></p><div
                  style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24"/>
                  <td valign="top" width="24">(b)</td>
                  <td colspan="4" valign="top" width="264">
                  <p class="Justify10Point">$30,600,000 shall be used for Local Assistance for the Clean Hydrogen Grants Program.</s></p><div
                  style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div>
                  </td>
                  <td valign="bottom" width="80"/>
                  </tr>
                  </tbody>
                  </table>
                  </caml:Content>
