                     <tr>
                        <td valign="top" width="24"></td>
                        <td valign="top" width="24">3.</td>
                        <td colspan="5" valign="top" width="288">
                           <div style="">The Director of Finance may authorize a short-term cash loan of up to $15,000,000 from the Underground Storage Tank Cleanup
                              Fund to provide cashflow needed to support operational costs that will be covered by fee revenue received by the end of the
                              fiscal year. The cash loan shall be subject to the terms and conditions for repayment as may be prescribed by the Department
                              of Finance. Interest charges may be waived pursuant to subdivision (e) of Section 16314 of the Government Code. For purposes
                              of the budgetary and legal bases of accounting and budgeting, the principal amount of any loans made pursuant to this provision
                              shall not be considered
                              			 part of the balance of the fund that receives the loan, nor shall it be deducted from the balance of the fund from which
                              the loan is made. These loans are considered cashflow loans for temporary cash shortages and shall not constitute budgetary
                              loans, revenues, or expenditures. The Department of Finance shall make the final determination of the budgetary and accounting
                              transactions and treatments to ensure proper implementation of this provision pursuant to Section 13344 of the Government
                              Code.
                           </div>
